.IX Title "Lucy::Plan::FullTextType 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Plan::FullTextType 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Plan::FullTextType \- Full\-text search field type.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 9
\&    my $easyanalyzer = Lucy::Analysis::EasyAnalyzer\->new(
\&        language => \*(Aqen\*(Aq,
\&    );
\&    my $type = Lucy::Plan::FullTextType\->new(
\&        analyzer => $easyanalyzer,
\&    );
\&    my $schema = Lucy::Plan::Schema\->new;
\&    $schema\->spec_field( name => \*(Aqtitle\*(Aq,   type => $type );
\&    $schema\->spec_field( name => \*(Aqcontent\*(Aq, type => $type );
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Lucy::Plan::FullTextType is an implementation of
FieldType tuned for “full text search”.
.PP
Full text fields are associated with an
Analyzer, which is used to tokenize and
normalize the text so that it can be searched for individual words.
.PP
For an exact-match, single value field type using character data, see
StringType.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 8
\&    my $type = Lucy::Plan::FullTextType\->new(
\&        analyzer      => $analyzer,    # required
\&        boost         => 2.0,          # default: 1.0
\&        indexed       => 1,            # default: true
\&        stored        => 1,            # default: true
\&        sortable      => 1,            # default: false
\&        highlightable => 1,            # default: false
\&    );
.Ve
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBanalyzer\fR \- An Analyzer.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBboost\fR \- floating point per-field boost.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBindexed\fR \- boolean indicating whether the field should be indexed.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBstored\fR \- boolean indicating whether the field should be stored.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsortable\fR \- boolean indicating whether the field should be sortable.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBhighlightable\fR \- boolean indicating whether the field should be
highlightable.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS set_highlightable
.IX Subsection "set_highlightable"
.Vb 1
\&    $full_text_type\->set_highlightable($highlightable);
.Ve
.PP
Indicate whether to store data required by
Highlighter for excerpt selection and search
term highlighting.
.SS highlightable
.IX Subsection "highlightable"
.Vb 1
\&    my $bool = $full_text_type\->highlightable();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor for “highlightable” property.
.SS get_analyzer
.IX Subsection "get_analyzer"
.Vb 1
\&    my $analyzer = $full_text_type\->get_analyzer();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor for the type’s analyzer.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Plan::FullTextType isa Lucy::Plan::TextType isa Lucy::Plan::FieldType isa Clownfish::Obj.
